      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "The natriuretic hormone peptide (NHP)(99-126), a C-terminal peptide of pro-atrial natriuretic factor (proANF), induces bronchodilatory effects in people with asthma. Recently, another plasmid-encoded C-terminal peptide, pNHP(73-102), was shown to induce a long-lasting bronchoprotective effect in a mouse model of allergic asthma."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "This study was carried out to determine the role of lung epithelial cells in the bronchoprotective and anti-inflammatory activity of these peptides."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Human type II alveolar epithelial cells (A549) and normal human bronchial epithelial (NHBE) cells were transfected with pNHP(73-102) to test the effect of this peptide on activation of these cells. After transfection, cells were analyzed for changes in Ca(++) and nitric oxide (NO) levels. Also, activation of NFkappaB and the extracellularly regulated kinase (ERK) 1, 2 signaling pathway was examined by luciferase reporter assay and phosphorylation studies respectively."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Analysis of intracellular Ca(++) levels in pNHP(73-102) -transfected A549 or NHBE showed that the peptide increases release. This Ca(++) release was accompanied by an increase in the production of NO. Also, overexpression of pNHP(73-102), but not pVAX control, in phorbol myristate acetate-activated A549 cells resulted in a significant decrease in expression of a cotransfected nuclear factorkappaB (NFkappaB)-luciferase reporter. Similarly, pNHP(73-102) decreased TNF-alpha-induced NFkappaB activation in NHBE cells. Furthermore, NHP(73-102) but not atrial natriuretic peptide decreased phosphorylation of Erk-1, 2 in A549 cells."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Overexpression of pNHP(73-102) in epithelial cells causes increased production of intracellular Ca(++) and NO, with a concomitant decrease in activation of NFkappaB and ERK1, 2. These results suggest a bronchodilatory and anti-inflammatory activity of this peptide."
        }
      ]},
